    fix(config): DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACE now selects the namespace (DF-0926-04)
    
    The documented per-agent isolation variable had ZERO readers in src/: every
    agent configured per docs/guide/ai-configure.md or the mcp-client example
    silently wrote to the config's defaultNamespace. Reproduced live first —
    `node bin/duckbrain.js stdio` with DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACE=dogfood-examples and
    `remember` answered `"namespace":"cfg-default"` (the config's default).
    
    PATH A (honor the variable), not Path B (delete the docs). The promise is the
    useful one — one DuckBrain instance, one namespace per agent — and honoring it
    is strictly additive: with the variable unset every surface resolves exactly as
    before, so no existing deployment changes behaviour. Path B would leave the
    users who already set the variable in the same silent shared-`default` state,
    just without a doc claiming otherwise.
    
    One resolution point:
    - src/config/index.ts applyEnvOverrides() reads DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACE (trimmed;
      blank/whitespace = unset) and overrides the file's defaultNamespace for THIS
      process only. Never persisted: updateConfig() merges against readFileConfig()
      (GAP-007), so an env-pinned agent cannot rewrite a shared config — asserted
      by a test and observed live (a 3-run CLI probe left the file byte-identical).
    - Every consumer that already resolves through the config inherits it:
      mcp/tools/shared.ts resolveNamespaceName (remember/recall/forget/search/
      squash/list_keys), the CLI (getDefaultNamespace), query/search-index/
      embeddings, git/remote.
    - src/http/routes/memories.ts: the six per-route `?namespace= || "default"`
      fallbacks AND the DB-GAP-031 grant resolver now share ONE
      resolveRequestNamespace() built on resolveNamespaceName. HTTP previously
      ignored both the env var and the config's defaultNamespace; sharing the
      resolver also removes the risk of the grant check grading a different
      namespace than the route touches.
    - src/http/routes/keys.ts: same resolver for /api/keys and /api/keys/flat.
    
    Effective order: explicit param (MCP arg / --namespace= / ?namespace=) >
    DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACE > config defaultNamespace > "default".
    
    Docs: the order is now documented in docs/guide/ai-configure.md (+ its
    byte-identical twin docs/AI_CONFIGURE.md, kept in sync as they were at HEAD),
    examples/mcp-client/README.md, docs/guide/configuration.md,
    docs/guide/getting-started.md and the duckbrain-usage skill (pitfall 26
    rewritten — it recorded the old bug; version 1.11.0 -> 1.12.0).
    DUCKBRAIN_DATA_DIR: the docs called it "where to store memory files" and it is
    only the HTTP PID-file directory (src/utils/pidfile.ts); the store root is
    DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH. Corrected in the docs instead of overloading the
    variable here, because docker-compose.yml already sets DUCKBRAIN_DATA_DIR=/data
    — treating it as a store root would silently relocate storage for existing
    deployments. Also flagged in the env table (documented, not fixed, outside this
    row): DUCKBRAIN_UI_PORT / _GIT_REMOTE / _LOG_LEVEL have no readers either.
    
    Tests (14 new, all green):
    - src/config/namespace-env-df092604.test.ts (8): env overrides the file, blank
      is ignored, whitespace trimmed, never persisted across updateConfig(), and the
      full precedence chain through resolveNamespaceName.
    - src/cli/namespace-env-df092604.test.ts (6): REAL subprocesses — stdio MCP via
      the SDK client (the response echoes the env namespace and the row is on disk
      under it), explicit-argument precedence, the CLI (`remember --wait`) with the
      env var set AND unset (config fallback control), and a scratch HTTP daemon on
      an ephemeral port with --auth=none whose POST without ?namespace= lands in the
      env namespace while an un-parameterized GET reads it back (the 404 from the
      config namespace is the discriminator).
    - RED proof: with src/config/index.ts + the two route files restored from HEAD,
      8 of the 14 fail (the env-ignored assertions) and the 6 controls still pass;
      the fixed files were restored with a sha256 check.
    
    Gates:
    - npx tsc --noEmit: exit 0
    - npx vitest run src/http/: 45 files / 296 tests passed (route change)
    - npx vitest run: 181 files, 1444/1444 TESTS PASSED. 0-2 files report a failure
      ONLY inside a pre-existing afterAll assertion that the repo-root
      duckbrain.config.json is byte-identical across the run (retr003+retr011 in one
      run, gap024 in the next, all passing 19/19 in isolation). That file is
